  "text": "**Argentina lost their attacking outlet, then their defensive security—not simply possession.** Acuña replacing Di María at 64' made the left side more defensive; afterward, Argentina’s pass share fell from 48.2% in the preceding window to 31.6%. That supports a loss of control, though it doesn’t prove the substitution caused it. Their attempted escape through Tagliafico and Acuña broke down under pressure. France then introduced Camavinga and Coman at 71', adding fresh options. [[ev:sb:3869685:2355]] [[seq:sb:3869685:s134]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2660]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2661]]\n\n**The decisive collapse was in chance prevention.** Argentina recovered to 58.4% pass share in the later window but generated only 0.02 xG against France’s 0.897. Mbappé’s penalty at 80' and equaliser at 81' punished that fragile control. Around the detected turning point, Argentina’s field tilt dropped from 58.1% to 28.5%: they could circulate the ball, but increasingly couldn’t keep play away from their own goal or threaten France. [[ev:sb:3869685:2928]] [[ev:sb:3869685:2987]] [[ev:sb:3869685:3037]]",
